#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186292527 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b466bd78-724b-51b2-8fee-7991bf7b60d2" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Using the Squared Cosine Variant of the Cosine Double-Angle Formula"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "502d17d5-be5c-562d-b871-8fe82e0a0635" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3\\pi}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292529}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "502d17d5-be5c-562d-b871-8fe82e0a0635" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3\\pi}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292529} :answer-field/id #uuid "71ce5d0d-4571-5944-be10-5bb24292d2d9" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292528}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "444c0bb0-6bb6-571a-b71e-29c116d1b48a" :question/math-academy-id "q-348735" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }6{cos}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Here, we use the double-angle formula for cosine that involves the ${cos}^{2}⁡x$ term, given by\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x=2{cos}^{2}⁡x-1.\n$$\n\n \n\nRearranging, we have\n\n$$\n2{cos}^{2}⁡x=\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+1.\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides by $3,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n6{cos}^{2}⁡x=3(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+1).\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }6{cos}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }3(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={(\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+3x)|}_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =[\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\pi )+3\\pi ]-[\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi )+3\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{2}] \\\\  & =3\\pi -\\frac{3\\pi }{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\pi }{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
